# Citation metadata for capa.
# Schema: https://citation-file-format.github.io
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "capa: control and DAQ for a controlled-atmosphere pyrolysis instrument"
message: "If you use capa in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bellamy
    given-names: Grayson
    email: gbellamy@umd.edu
    affiliation: University of Maryland
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GraysonBellamy/capa"
url: "https://graysonbellamy.github.io/capa/"
abstract: >-
  capa is a control and data-acquisition application for a custom
  cone-calorimeter-class lab instrument used for controlled-atmosphere
  pyrolysis. It drives heaters, mass-flow controllers, balances,
  NI-DAQ, and USB/IR cameras through async-first device libraries and
  records every run as a self-contained on-disk bundle (config, method,
  calibration snapshot, events, samples, video).
keywords:
  - cone-calorimeter
  - controlled-atmosphere-pyrolysis
  - data-acquisition
  - laboratory-instrument
  - astm-e1354
  - iso-5660
